{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310571,"nonce":"l9iVHLvb9NjKN9HANXg9Opisr8o=","title":"OPEN cross-module Dynamic-object \u0026 reflection bugs (2026-06-29): a class instance passed to an imported instance method's Dynamic param ...","message":"**Found 2026-06-29 building rayzor.test.Spec (an imported stdlib framework that\nstress-tests cross-module Dynamic). All verified by probe. Each works\nSAME-module and breaks CROSS-module (value/Class/type args crossing into an\nimported module). These are the dangerous cross-module subsystem\n([[bugs_import_xmodule_member_resolution]], [[bugs_cross_module_dispatch_complexity]]).**\n\nWhat DOES work cross-module (landed): PRIMITIVE Int/Float/Bool → Dynamic param\nboxing (commit 195e873e, `coerce_arg_to_dynamic_param` + `boxing_param_types` in\nast_lowering — narrow on purpose). Class instances are pointers and pass fine as\nRECEIVERS / through STATIC calls. `Reflect.field`/`fields`/`length` via a STATIC\ncross-module call works. Reference `==` via a STATIC cross-module call works.\n\nOPEN bugs (NOT fixed; do NOT build features on them):\n1. **Class instance → cross-module INSTANCE-method Dynamic param arrives VOID.**\n   `p.inst(fooInstance)` where `inst(o:Dynamic)` → inside, `o` is null (`Std.string(o)`==\"void\").\n   ROOT (diagnosed 2026-06-29 via MIR): the MIR is CORRECT — it passes `inst($this, $foo)`\n   and the body reads `Std.string($1)`. But the class arg is passed with static type\n   `Foo` to a `Dynamic` param (NO coercion — classes aren't in the value-types coerce\n   set), and that arg/param TYPE MISMATCH drops the arg (→ null) at the cross-module\n   instance-method boundary. Contrast: an Int arg works because the coerce wraps it in\n   `Cast→Dynamic` so its type matches the param; a String arg arrives as a raw ptr\n   (garbles, not null). STATIC calls handle the mismatch (raw class arg survives);\n   INSTANCE calls don't. Full fix needs class-arg→Dynamic coercion AND the box-id\n   consistency fix below (else typeof/isOfType on the result still wrong) — converges\n   on the higher-risk box-id change that also touches downcast/cast. NOT least-magnitude.\n2. **`Reflect`-based deep compare on primitives crashes cross-module.** Static\n   `fieldCount`/`fieldVal` worked, but a recursive `deepEquals(5,5)` (Reflect.fields\n   on a boxed primitive) SIGSEGVs cross-module.\n3. **`Std.isOfType(obj, Cls)` returns FALSE for the correct class cross-module**\n   (same-module true). Class identity lost across the boundary — likely the\n   Class\u003cT\u003e arg or the obj header type_id mismatches across modules.\n4. **`Type.typeof(v)` on a Dynamic → W0020 SIGILL trap-stub** — TRAP FIXED\n   2026-06-29 (4bd2072f). NOT cross-module (mis-filed): fired for ANY\n   `Type.typeof(v)` where `v:Dynamic`, same-module too. Root: `lower_type_typeof_call`\n   did `box_value_for_dynamic(...)?`, but that returns `None` for an already-Dynamic\n   value, and `?` dropped the result → \"Return with no value\" stub. Fix: a\n   statically-Dynamic arg is already a Dynamic pointer — use it directly.\n   RESIDUAL (deeper, open): a class instance in a Dynamic reports `TUnknown` — the\n   reference box tags with the TAST `TypeId` (e.g. 174), not the deterministic\n   runtime class id (object header, e.g. 478025335) that `haxe_type_typeof_value`\n   looks up. Primitives (TInt/TFloat/TBool) now correct. Test: test_typeof_dynamic.hx.\n\nConsequence: rayzor.test.Spec deliberately offers ONLY value (`expect`:\nInt/Float/Bool/structural-by-Std.string) + String (`expectStr`, typed). Object\nmatchers (toBe/toEqualDeep/toBeInstanceOf/toBeOfType) were probed, all four broke\ncross-module, and were NOT added (would be silent hidden errors).\n\nAlso OPEN / decided: **String→Dynamic call-arg boxing is UNSAFE** — boxing a\nString arg to `trace`/`Sys.println` (type-specialized sinks that consume a RAW\nString pointer) breaks them AND nue's own output. So String stays raw at call\nargs; `Std.string` on a raw-String-Dynamic is the unresolved root (needs a tagged\nrepr both sinks and Std.string accept). That's why the framework's String path is\nthe TYPED `expectStr`, not `expect(Dynamic)`.\n\nnue impact: LOW — nue uses typed Tensor/QTensor + Sys.println, 0 `@:native`\nexterns, no cross-module Dynamic reflection/downcasts. These bite framework/\nreflection-heavy code, not nue's hot path. Fixing them is a focused\ncross-module-resolution effort (run the full haxe suite as the regression gate;\nthe broad first attempt regressed 20 SIMD/quant/closure tests).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_cross_module_dynamic_object_reflection` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}